-- The arity error of a call BY POSITION says how to leave an input to its
-- default (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md section 4.2, U1: R8 rule 1 is kept,
-- and the error names the WITH form; the wording is assumed, not ruled).
-- It says so only when the callee declares a TYPICALLY default for an input.

GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
GIVETH A NUMBER
`last input defaulted` MEANS base TIMES rate

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 1
      b IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2
GIVETH A NUMBER
`both defaulted` MEANS a PLUS b

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`no defaults` MEANS x PLUS y

-- One short, and the callee has a default: the error shows the WITH form.
#EVAL `last input defaulted` 10

-- Every input has a default, and none is given by name: the error shows the form
-- with the first input as the example, and says "to their defaults".
#EVAL `both defaulted` 5

-- No input has a default: the message is what it was before.
#EVAL `no defaults` 5

-- More inputs than the callee takes: not a matter of a default, and unchanged.
#EVAL `last input defaulted` 1 2 3
